    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All **45 tests pass** with 0 failures and 0 errors. **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers entirely.\n\nThe change was localized to one method in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, because everything the spec calls out as \"built from the customerCode\" already reads the stored `customerCode` (or shares the same region derivation) and therefore follows automatically:\n\n**`generateCustomerCode(Owner owner)`** (rewritten):\n- **REGION** = `OwnerLocality.of(city, postcode)` \u2014 the postcode-first region derivation, which is the *same* one that produces the owner's `locality`. This satisfies \"REGION derived from the postcode\" and keeps the identity's region and the locality field consistent.\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The telephone is already normalized by the time this runs.\n- No more `findAllOwners()` sequence count \u2014 the code is a pure function of the owner's own region and identity.\n\nI added a small `sha256Hex(String)` helper and refactored `householdIdFor` to reuse it (removing the duplicated digest-to-hex loop).\n\nEverything downstream now uses the new identity with no further edits:\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) \u2014 reads `customerCode` \u2192 Cp14 \u2713\n- **Check digit** (Luhn over `customerCode` digits) \u2014 Cp31 \u2713\n- **Create audit record** (logs `customerCode`) \u2014 now emits e.g. `customerCode=NSW-779D69B5` \u2192 Cp21 \u2713\n- **Locality** derivation \u2014 unchanged region logic, still shared with the identity \u2192 Cp17, Cp30 \u2713\n\nVerified by the acceptance suite: the new-format checkpoints (Cp09, Cp16, Cp32) and all dependent ones pass, and no previously-passing test regressed.",
